  m_Name: FeatureDefinition_SneakAttack
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: CRPG.Actors::CRPG.Actors.FeatureDefinition
  id: feature-sneak-attack
  displayName: Sneak Attack
  description: 'Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack if you have advantage on the attack roll. The attack must use a finesse or a ranged weapon. You don''t need advantage on the attack roll if another enemy of the target is within 5 feet of it, that enemy isn''t incapacitated, and you don''t have disadvantage on the attack roll. The extra damage is 1d6 at levels 1-2, and increases to 2d6 at level 3 and beyond (SRD5 progresses further at higher levels, out of scope here). INERT: this feature grants no mechanical modifiers. Its real trigger -- advantage on the attack roll, OR an ally within 5 ft of the target -- is attacker-side/adjacency combat state that no effect type in this engine can currently see (ConditionalEffect only inspects the target''s own ConditionDefinitions). Authored ahead of a future ''conditional bonus damage on an attack'' effect hook.'
  modifiers: []
  grantedAbilityIds: []
  grantedResources: []
  grantedProficiencies: []
  choices: []
